Integer coefficients for the element routines in this addon.


List of the coefficients
------------------------

  1-150: all relevant integer coefficients from the stokes & viscoelastic add-on
151-200: reserved for diffuse_interface add-on
201-250: reserved for inertia add-on
251-300: reserved for generalized Stokes add-on


301 Time integration scheme:
    1: first-order, semi-implicit BDF1 (Euler)
    2: second-order, semi-implicit BDF2 with convection velocity prediction
    3: first-order, implicit BDF1
    4: second-order, implicit BDF2

302 Position in oldvectors%s of the solution vector containing the velocity and
    pressure at the previous time step n. Older (step n-1,...) solution values
    are stored sequentially. A Value of 0 means default = 1.

303 Position in oldvectors%s of the _prediction_ for the solution vector
    (velocity and pressure) for the next time step n+1.
    A Value of 0 means default = 1.
    NOTE: this is only used for the convection velocity in the semi-implicit
          time-integration methods and coefficients%i(304)=0.

304 The predicted convection velocity in semi-implicit time-integration methods
    is:
    0: taken from the sysvector as given by coefficients%i(303) (default). In
       this case, the user must compute uhat=2un-unm1 in the main routine for
       the second-order method.
    1: computed on element level from the sysvector(s) given by
       coefficients%i(302).

305 Position in oldvectors%s of the iteration solution for velocity and
    pressure. A Value of 0 means default = 1. This is currently only used
    for the implicit routine implicit_pressure_ce_elem.

306 Indicates whether the time-derivative term in the pressure equation
    will be included in the routine implicit_pressure_ce_elem:
    0 yes
    1 No, the time-derivative term is excluded from the system.
      Excluding the time-derivative term will only build the Jacobian
      of the convection term and (minus) the right-hand side of the pressure
      equation. The main reason for for excluding the time-derivative term is
      to be able to perform Newton-Raphson iteration for the steady state.

307 Constraint number of the integral pressure constraint to set the level of
    the pressure field.

308 Indicates which integral pressure constraint is used (see Userguide):
    1 Constraint F1(p) = \int exp[(p-p0)/K] dV - V0 = 0
    2 Constraint F2(p) = K F1(p)
    3 Constraint \bar F1(p) = \int { exp[(p-p0)/K]-1 } dV = 0
    4 Constraint \bar F2(p) = K \bar F1(p)
    5 Constraint \int (p - p_level) dV = 0
    NOTES:
    - 1 and 2 require V0=coefficients%r(254) to be set.
    - 3 and 4 does not use V0=coefficients%r(254), but can only be used if
      the current volume V remains constant and equal to V0.
    - 5 can be used in any incompressible flow with Newton-Raphson iteration
      where pressure increments (\Delta p) are computed.

309-350: Reserved for future use. Set to zero for future compatibility.
